            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0147" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/323</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the Division
                        of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-04">May 4, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During a call from the Turkish Ambassador this morning he again inquired as to
                    what, if any, developments had occurred in the proposed sending of a
                    representative from this Government to confer with certain notables of the
                    Islamic world. I told the Ambassador that nothing had happened since our last
                    conversation.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador said that he desired again to make it clear, and trusted that he
                    had sufficiently emphasized during previous conversations, that in case such a
                    proposal came to fruition Turkey would find herself in an embarrassing position,
                    either if she were approached or if she were ignored. He did, however, make the
                    suggestion today that if the Turkish President were directly approached in the
                    matter he might find it possible to influence, through the Director of the
                    Bureau of Religious Affairs, the prayers given in the mosques of the country so
                    that the idea of world peace might be duly emphasized.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[The plan for consultation with leaders of the Eastern Orthodox and
                        Mohammedan faiths was abandoned.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
